    "lawCode": "Amd §22, Chap 352 of 2005; amd §8, Chap 430 of 2006; amd §27, Chap 378 of 2007",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8796\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 352 of the laws of 2005, amending the education\nlaw relating to implementation of the federal individuals with disabili-\nties education improvement act of 2004; to amend chapter 430 of the laws\nof 2006, amending the education law relating to implementation of the\nfederal individuals with disabilities education improvement act of 2004;\nand to amend chapter 378 of the laws of 2007, amending the education law\nrelating to the implementation of the federal individuals with disabili-\nties education improvement act of 2004, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend, for three years, provisions that\nconform state education law to the federal Individuals with Disabilities\nEducation Act (IDEA) of 2004 in order to ensure that the State will\ncontinue to be in compliance with federal IDEA requirements through the\n2026-2027 school year.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n\nSections 1, 2, and 3 of this bill would extend for three years, until\nJune 30, 2027, provisions of the Education Law relating to the implemen-\ntation of IDEA.\n\nSection 4 provides that the effective date shall take effect immediate-\nly, provided, however, if this act shall have become a law after June\n30, 2024 it shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect on and after June 30, 2024.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would extend provisions of the Education Law that conform\nstate statute to the federal Individuals with Disabilities Act of 2004.\nFederal funding for students with disabilities is contingent upon\ncompliance with the extension of IDEA. The current provisions of law\nwill sunset on June 30, 2024. Without an extender, the State's allo-\ncation of funds under IDEA could be in jeopardy. This bill extends\nprovisions of the Education Law for three years until June 30, 2027 to\nensure the State continues to remain compliant and receive federal fund-\ning.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided, however, if this act\nshall have become a law after June 30, 2021 it shall take effect imme-\ndiately and shall be deemed to have been in full force and effect on and\nafter June 30, 2021.\n",
